WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.150
Will we see Drax, Nebula, and all the rest
after the Guardians of the Galaxy drop their

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.339
third adventure?

00:00:06.535 --> 00:00:09.446
And what's the deal with Will Poulter's Adam
Warlock?

00:00:09.446 --> 00:00:14.423
Here's what you need to know about what seems
to be James Gunn's final film in the MCU.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.380
After a controversial Phase 4, the MCU's Phase
5 kicked off in March with "Ant-Man and the

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.760
Wasp: Quantumania".

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.519
The film set up some huge stakes for the MCU
by introducing the new big bad, Kang the Conqueror.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:32.320
However, after all that multiverse madness,
Phase 5 will shift its focus from the Quantum

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.559
Realm to Knowhere as the saga of Star-Lord
continues.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:39.790
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" has had a
long road to theaters.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:44.730
As everyone knows, director James Gunn was
fired from the "Guardians" movies in 2018,

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.840
after a politically charged controversy involving
old tweets.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.140
Of course, he was eventually rehired by Disney,
and after joining forces with DC for "The

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:58.100
Suicide Squad" and "Peacemaker," Gunn was
able to focus on getting Drax, Mantis, and

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.969
Nebula back on the big screen.

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:04.810
With all that drama out of the way, "Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3" is finally in the can.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.880
So, when can we expect to see these adorable
losers and murderous misfits?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.720
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" will return
in all its action-packed, emotional, musical

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.860
glory on May 5, 2023.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:22.620
There are two trailers for "Guardians of the
Galaxy Vol. 3" as of the making of this video,

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.229
and they promise to bring hilarity, horror,
heroics, but mostly heartbreak.

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:32.096
The first trailer opens with the Guardians
landing on a strange planet filled with humanoid animals.

00:01:32.096 --> 00:01:36.229
It's possible this could be a combination
of two different Marvel worlds — Counter-Earth

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.939
and Halfworld.

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:42.390
In the comics, Counter-Earth is a place created
by the High Evolutionary, while Halfworld

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:47.560
is a planet filled with anthropomorphic animals,
all the result of horrific experiments.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.100
After Drax makes a hilarious and disastrous
first impression on the locals, we get a glimpse

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.909
of the Guardians donning "2001: A Space Odyssey"-inspired
space suits, baby Rocket about to suffer at

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:02.328
the hands of the High Evolutionary, and our
heroes preparing to make a final stand.

00:02:02.328 --> 00:02:08.513
"We have been running our whole lives."

00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:12.345
"Pete, I'm done running."

00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:16.450
While the emotions are high, the trailer does
end with Peter Quill and Drax debating the

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.290
appropriate number of people to kill, showing
these guys will always be our lovable criminals.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.440
The second trailer, released during Super
Bowl 2023, starts off by highlighting the

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.110
sticky dynamics between Peter and this new
Gamora, who has no memory of him whatsoever.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.750
As a result, she doesn't exactly reciprocate
his affectionate feelings.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.900
We also get a much better look at the High
Evolutionary and his sinister intentions,

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.590
which in his mind is to make the perfect society.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.855
But his most famous experiment, Rocket Raccoon,
has a different take on the situation.

00:02:45.855 --> 00:02:48.489
"He didn't want to make things perfect.

00:02:50.107 --> 00:02:52.570
He just hated things the way they are."

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:57.040
It also gives us several new shots of Adam
Warlock in combat with the Guardians, going

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.486
toe to toe with Drax in what's sure to be
a nail-biter of a battle.

00:03:00.898 --> 00:03:05.422
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" was filmed
immediately after "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:03:05.422 --> 00:03:10.860
Meanwhile, director James Gunn took on an
extra project, making the 2022 "Holiday Special"

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.950
at the same time as the movie.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.890
Gunn confirmed that the Disney+ special is
part of the Marvel canon, and that it actually

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.760
sets the stage quite nicely for "Vol. 3."

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.459
In "The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday Special,"
we learn several key details about the future

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:26.430
of our scrappy band of space pirates.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:31.269
Following their appearance in "Love and Thunder"
the remaining team of Quill, Drax, Mantis,

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:35.599
Nebula, Rocket, and Groot have moved on to
continue protecting the galaxy.

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:39.920
The "Holiday Special" revealed that they settled
on Knowhere, buying the severed Celestial

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.120
head that once served as a base for Tivan
the Collector.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.280
In addition to seeing some bizarre gift giving,
which included Mantis and Drax kidnapping

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:52.341
Kevin Bacon for Quill and Nebula stealing
Bucky Barnes' vibranium arm for Rocket, we

00:03:52.341 --> 00:03:54.370
learn they've acquired a new ship called the
Bowie.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.849
Most importantly of all, though, it's revealed
that Mantis and Quill are actually paternal

00:03:57.849 --> 00:03:59.090
half-siblings.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:04.363
Peter is also still visibly mourning the loss
of Gamora, who died at Thanos' hands in "Infinity War."

00:04:04.363 --> 00:04:08.233
And, even though an alternate version of her
traveled through time to fight alongside them

00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:12.900
in "Endgame," she has no memory of Peter and
ditches the Guardians, leaving Star-Lord with

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.909
a broken heart.

00:04:14.198 --> 00:04:18.079
We know the Guardians are adjusting to their
new lives, with villain-turned-hero Nebula

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:20.817
settling into being an official member of
Quill's team.

00:04:20.817 --> 00:04:25.730
According to the official plot synopsis, the
Guardians don't get much down time, as things

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:28.270
"are upended by the echoes of Rocket's turbulent
past."

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.729
The synopsis goes on:

00:04:29.729 --> 00:04:33.560
"Peter Quill, still reeling from the loss
of Gamora, must rally his team around him

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.449
on a dangerous mission to save Rocket's life
— a mission that, if not completed successfully,

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:41.840
could quite possibly lead to the end of the
Guardians as we know them."

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.229
This confirms that "Vol. 3" will be focused
on Rocket's backstory, something Gunn has

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:48.099
been hinting at for a long time.

00:04:48.099 --> 00:04:50.880
What element of Rocket's past is coming back
to haunt him?

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.760
All signs point to the villainous High Evolutionary,
who's intent on creating a perfect society

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:59.160
of evolved beings by whatever torturous means
necessary.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.090
We also know that Adam Warlock, a powerful
figure created by the Guardians' enemy, the

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.240
High Priestess Ayesha, will factor into the
story.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.919
In short, our heroes are really up against
it.

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:13.368
Thankfully, they won't be doing it alone,
with the past version of Gamora making her return.

00:05:13.368 --> 00:05:17.750
She's been off leading the Ravagers, filling
the power vacuum left after "Vol. 2."

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.900
But things could get complicated if "Vol.
3" sets up a love triangle among Gamora, Peter,

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.030
and Nebula.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:28.398
This Gamora has no feelings for Peter, while
he and Nebula have been growing closer.

00:05:28.625 --> 00:05:33.673
As you might expect, all the usual suspects
are returning to play their respective Guardians roles.

00:05:33.673 --> 00:05:39.389
Chris Pratt is back as Peter Quill, aka Star-Lord,
and Zoe Saldaña returns as a version of Gamora

00:05:39.389 --> 00:05:41.360
that doesn't remember her old friends.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.210
Bradley Cooper voices Rocket Raccoon, Vin
Diesel portrays Groot, and Dave Bautista is

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.430
back as Drax the Destroyer.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.970
Rounding out the old guard, we've got Pom
Klementieff as Star-Lord's psychic half-sister,

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:56.430
Mantis, and Karen Gillan as the dead-eyed
assassin with a secret heart of gold, Nebula.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:00.910
And hopefully, Sean Gunn's Kraglin will have
figured out how to use Yondu's arrow by now.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.960
However, there's a new Guardian in town: Cosmo
the Space Dog, the telekinetic, talking pooch

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.460
who first debuted in the "Holiday Special."

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:13.150
She'll be voiced by Maria Bakalova, who earned
international acclaim and an Oscar nomination

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:17.060
for her turn as Tutar Sagdiyev in "Borat Subsequent
Moviefilm."

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.740
On the antagonist side of the aisle, we've
got Chukwudi Iwuji as the High Evolutionary.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:26.310
Iwuji is no stranger to working with James
Gunn, as he previously starred as the enigmatic

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:29.590
Clemson Murn in HBO Max's "Peacemaker" series.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.500
Will Poulter will portray Adam Warlock, a
guy who's going to give the Guardians a pretty

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.500
hard time.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:38.810
You'll no doubt remember Poulter for his work
in projects like "Midsommar," and "Black Mirror."

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:42.280
We've also got some pretty big names appearing
in smaller side roles.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:46.550
Elizabeth Debicki will be reprising her part
as the High Priestess Ayesha, the high and

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:51.319
mighty creator of Adam Warlock, and Sylvester
Stallone returns as Ravager Stakar.

00:06:51.319 --> 00:06:55.440
Michael Rosenbaum of "Smallville" fame is
coming back as the crystalline Martinex, and

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:01.879
we can also expect to see Daniela Melchior
of "The Suicide Squad" and Nico Santos of "Superstore."

00:07:01.982 --> 00:07:05.449
Some MCU heroes are inextricably tied with
their directors.

00:07:05.449 --> 00:07:09.979
At this point, it's hard to separate Thor
from Taika Waititi, Ryan Coogler is connected

00:07:09.979 --> 00:07:14.759
to the world of Wakanda, and Jon Watts shepherded
Spider-Man across all three films.

00:07:14.759 --> 00:07:19.080
However, when it comes to a director and their
respective super-franchise, perhaps no filmmaker

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.349
has left a bigger impact than James Gunn.

00:07:21.349 --> 00:07:26.348
He's guided the Guardians from the very beginning,
both writing the scripts and directing the films.

00:07:26.348 --> 00:07:30.070
In addition to the "Guardians" movies and
the "Holiday Special," Gunn is famous for

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:33.550
his work at DC, having helmed "The Suicide
Squad" and "Peacemaker."

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:39.610
Then, of course, he became the DCU's version
of Kevin Feige, along with co-head Peter Safran.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:43.729
Talking about his love of the "Guardians"
franchise, the new DC Studios co-head spoke

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:46.419
to Deadline about his last Marvel project,
saying,

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:50.160
"The reason why I needed to finish this is
because I love the character of Rocket more

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.870
than any character I've ever dealt with before,
and I needed to finish his story, and that

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.300
is what 'Volume 3' is about.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:00.700
I absolutely needed to do it, and I think
we've done it in a spectacular way that I

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.206
can't wait for people to see."

00:08:02.206 --> 00:08:05.870
While we know "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.
3" will be the final "Guardians" movie with

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:10.009
director James Gunn and this line-up of heroes,
we don't know which characters will die or

00:08:10.009 --> 00:08:13.110
if any of them might come back in later MCU
movies.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:16.699
However, we do know for a fact there's one
actor who won't be returning.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:19.729
Sadly, it looks like Dave Bautista is done
with playing Drax.

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:25.300
He announced he was officially moving on from
the literal-minded Destroyer in 2021 on "Ellen,"

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.699
telling the talk show host,

00:08:26.699 --> 00:08:30.580
"I'm going to be 54 years old by the time
'Guardians 3' comes out.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:33.000
The shirtless thing is getting harder and
harder for me."

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.900
While that may indeed be a factor when it
comes to moving on from Marvel, Bautista has

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.709
given other reasons for his departure of a
more personal nature.

00:08:40.709 --> 00:08:44.360
Talking with GQ, Bautista elaborated a bit
more on his decision saying,

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.950
"I'm so grateful for Drax.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:46.950
I love him.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:47.950
But there's a relief.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.210
It wasn't all pleasant.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.100
It was hard playing that role.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:53.020
The makeup process was beating me down.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:57.410
And I just don't know if I want Drax to be
my legacy — it's a silly performance, and

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.339
I want to do more dramatic stuff."

00:08:59.339 --> 00:09:01.347
"Will you make a choice?"

00:09:01.347 --> 00:09:06.610
Fans can't wait to see what the wrestler-turned-legit-thespian
does next, as he's proven he's got serious

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:12.161
range with roles in films like "Glass Onion,"
"Blade Runner 2049," and "Knock at the Cabin."

00:09:12.597 --> 00:09:16.230
With the "Guardians of the Galaxy" franchise
saying goodbye to Dave Bautista's Drax the

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.040
Destroyer, it really is the end of an era.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.399
Unfortunately, it looks like he might not
be the only member of the Guardians who fans

00:09:22.399 --> 00:09:23.600
will have to bid farewell to.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.839
In a cryptic Instagram post which celebrated
the end of filming for "Guardians of the Galaxy

00:09:27.839 --> 00:09:33.160
Vol. 3" back in May 2022, Scottish actor Karen
Gillan teased that Nebula's story might have

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.220
come to an end.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.399
She captioned alongside a photo from the set,

00:09:36.399 --> 00:09:41.131
"I don't know if Nebula will return beyond
this, it's possible that this is her final chapter.

00:09:41.131 --> 00:09:44.640
And if that's the case, then I just want to
say thank you to @jamesgunn for giving me

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.290
such an interesting, complex and fascinating
character to play.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:52.040
I have enjoyed this exploration more than
any other character I've played.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.460
That was one hell of a decade.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:54.460
Thanks for watching."

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:58.820
Whether Nebula is going to bite the dust in
dramatic fashion remains to be seen, since

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:03.130
Gillan's statement is rather ambiguous, but
this certainly could be her final foray across

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.360
the galaxy.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:08.410
Of course, you never really know if someone
is gone for good when it comes to the MCU.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.649
Just look at characters like Gamora and Loki.

00:10:10.649 --> 00:10:14.785
So if Gillan is open to it, Nebula may pop
up somewhere else in the future.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.640
All good things must come to an end, and unfortunately,
that also applies to the "Guardians of the

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.640
Galaxy" movies.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.410
It's been quite a journey since this motley
crew first appeared on the cinematic scene

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.410
in 2014.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.800
They've introduced us to some groovy mixtapes,
saved the world with dancing, fought Kurt

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.070
Russell, and kidnapped Kevin Bacon.

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:35.240
And now, in "Vol. 3," they'll be gearing up
for one last adventure as they attempt to

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:37.830
save Rocket from his traumatic past.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.910
Confirming it will be their last outing, director
James Gunn told Deadline,

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:45.250
"This is the end for us, the last time people
will see this team of Guardians."

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:49.250
That implies we may see some of the Guardians
again, or perhaps a different iteration of

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.920
the team will show up at some point.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.420
We're assuming that some of the Guardians
will simply fly off into the horizon.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.210
We're also assuming that some of them will
die.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.450
From the trailers, it looks like Rocket is
going to be in some serious trouble after

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.780
running across the High Evolutionary, and
based on Dave Bautista's comments about moving

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:09.040
on from the MCU, it looks like the Destroyer
might also be on the chopping block.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.399
However, fans shouldn't expect a bloodbath.

00:11:11.399 --> 00:11:14.256
As James Gunn said at Comic-Con in June 2022,

00:11:14.256 --> 00:11:16.030
"This is the end of that story.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.030
I'm sorry.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.030
Some stories have an end.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.500
It doesn't mean everybody dies."

00:11:19.814 --> 00:11:23.741
Based on the trailers, it seems like the High
Evolutionary will be the big bad of "Guardians

00:11:23.741 --> 00:11:25.200
of the Galaxy Vol. 3."

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.560
However, there's another force lurking in
the cosmos that might be an even bigger threat:

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.560
Adam Warlock.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.540
We've known he was coming since the post-credits
scene of "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2."

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.519
Early in the film, Rocket gets his greedy
little paws on some Anulax batteries that

00:11:38.519 --> 00:11:42.329
belong to the Sovereign, a race of genetically
modified, gold aliens.

00:11:42.329 --> 00:11:46.730
Consumed with vengeance, the High Priestess
Ayesha spends a good chunk of "Vol. 2" trying

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:50.990
to kill the Guardians, and when that doesn't
work out, she decides to create the perfect

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.579
superweapon: Adam Warlock.

00:11:52.849 --> 00:12:00.577
"More powerful, more beautiful, more capable
of destroying the Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:12:00.577 --> 00:12:05.200
Talking about this new superbeing, James Gunn
elaborated on Warlock a bit, telling Empire

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.060
the character's life purpose is a tad more
complicated than just wiping out our band

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.589
of music-loving heroes.

00:12:10.589 --> 00:12:11.980
That said, according to Gunn:

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.870
"He's definitely not a good guy.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:18.630
What we're seeing is the infant form of Warlock,
newly out of the cocoon, and he does not understand

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.690
life very well.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:21.459
He's basically a baby."

00:12:21.459 --> 00:12:24.839
So are there any details we can glean from
Warlock's comic book background that might

00:12:24.839 --> 00:12:27.350
help us understand the character going forward?

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:31.399
Created by Stan Lee and Jack Kirby, Adam Warlock
was made to be a perfect being by a group

00:12:31.399 --> 00:12:35.850
called the Enclave before he was found drifting
through space by the High Evolutionary.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:40.320
The space scientist essentially adopted Warlock
as his own son, giving him the Soul Stone

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:45.439
and sending him down as his representative
to Counter-Earth, a world of the High Evolutionary's making.

00:12:45.439 --> 00:12:50.233
So it's possible we might see some sort of
relationship between the two characters in "Vol. 3."

00:12:50.233 --> 00:12:54.743
Additionally, in the comics, Warlock was a
huge player in the "Infinity Gauntlet" storyline.

00:12:54.743 --> 00:12:59.330
He was instrumental in defeating Thanos, and
once it was all said and done, he became the

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.450
wielder of the bejeweled, reality-altering
glove.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:06.199
For a time, Warlock was also a member of the
Guardians of the Galaxy, so he has serious

00:13:06.199 --> 00:13:09.510
comic book connections to all the major players
in "Vol. 3."

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.500
Will he be a loyal Evolutionary acolyte in
the film, or will he eventually side with

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.500
the Guardians?

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.083
We'll see how that all plays out on May 5,
2023.

00:13:18.225 --> 00:13:21.850
The "Guardians of the Galaxy" franchise just
wouldn't be the same without the classic rock

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.920
soundtracks scoring each of the movies.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.870
James Gunn worked on these personally, listening
to hundreds of songs before creating the soundtrack

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.090
for the first movie.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:33.790
It sounds like we can look forward to a third
playlist even more powerful than its predecessors.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:34.970
Gunn told Entertainment Weekly,

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:39.640
"I worked twice as hard on this soundtrack
as I did on both the first two soundtracks combined."

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:43.600
Marvel fans got their first taste of the "Vol.
3" soundtrack in the trailers.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.720
The second trailer features Rainbow's "Since
You've Been Gone."

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:52.009
The 1976 rock song confirms that Gunn is bringing
back more '70s hits to the franchise.

00:13:52.009 --> 00:13:55.930
But he also confirmed that since the music
in this film is coming from the Zune MP3 player

00:13:55.930 --> 00:14:01.089
which Peter got from Kraglin at the end of
"Vol. 2," rather than his mom's old mixtapes.

00:14:01.089 --> 00:14:05.759
That would explain why a hit from 1996, "In
the Meantime" by Spacehog, is featured in

00:14:05.759 --> 00:14:07.784
the first trailer released for the film.

00:14:07.784 --> 00:14:11.589
Despite having life-or-death stakes for the
characters, "Guardians of the Galaxy" movies

00:14:11.589 --> 00:14:15.579
are known to be light-hearted, funny, musically
inclined superhero movies.

00:14:15.579 --> 00:14:18.019
At least, they have been so far.

00:14:18.019 --> 00:14:22.255
According to Gunn, the tone of "Vol. 3" is
going to be completely different from its predecessors.

00:14:22.255 --> 00:14:23.255
He told Deadline,

00:14:23.255 --> 00:14:28.754
"It's big; it's so, so big and dark, and different
from what people might be expecting it to be."

00:14:28.754 --> 00:14:33.000
Dave Bautista told Uproxx that this change
in tone is going to make the film great.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.339
"It's just so much better, so much deeper.

00:14:35.339 --> 00:14:36.699
It's so much more personal.

00:14:36.699 --> 00:14:39.880
And there's such a massive inspiring message
to this film."

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:43.589
Before even watching a full cut of the feature,
he confidently told the outlet that it's going

00:14:43.589 --> 00:14:45.779
to be the best of the three "Guardians" movies.

00:14:45.779 --> 00:14:49.800
That's certainly a lot to live up to, but
other cast members including Karen Gillan

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:54.200
and Pom Klementieff were also moved by the
heavier storyline, which we know will center

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.370
around Rocket but involve the rest of the
cast, too.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:01.279
Speaking to Digital Spy, Gillan admitted that
the script was so evocative that it brought

00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:02.880
her and Klementieff to tears.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:06.910
"We read it together and we both cried and
laughed, but there was full tears.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:11.745
It's incredible, I think it's James' strongest
work yet with the Guardians and it's just brilliant."

00:15:11.745 --> 00:15:13.635
"Now you're just making it sad!"

00:15:13.635 --> 00:15:17.589
However, Gillan made sure to mention that
there's plenty of that classic "Guardians"

00:15:17.589 --> 00:15:18.610
humor in the film too.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:23.930
Chukwudi Iwuji plays the High Evolutionary,
a powerful villain with virtually unlimited

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.470
intellectual power.

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:29.430
The character comes straight from the pages
of Stan Lee and Jack Kirby's comics, first

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:31.839
appearing in "Thor" #134.

00:15:31.839 --> 00:15:37.360
Iwuji is excited to bring the character to
the big screen, as he told Collider with great enthusiasm.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:40.709
"He is narcissistic, sociopathic, but very
charming.

00:15:40.709 --> 00:15:44.389
[...] There's something very Shakespearean
about him, there's something very emotionally

00:15:44.389 --> 00:15:47.580
dark about him, and he's a lot of fun on top
of all that."

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:52.339
However, his casting was unfortunately met
with a cruel racist backlash from some commenters

00:15:52.339 --> 00:15:53.529
on social media.

00:15:53.529 --> 00:15:58.440
One particular Instagram troll criticized
his portrayal of the High Evolutionary, insisting

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.440
the character is supposed to be white.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:04.790
However, director James Gunn took the opportunity
to speak out against those comments on Instagram.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:08.399
"I chose the best actor, period, and the best
person for the role.

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:13.800
I don't give a s--- what ethnicity Chukwudi
Iwuji is, so stop with your racist presumptions

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.880
on WHY he was chosen."

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:19.250
He also pointed out the character's look from
the comic books, adding,

00:16:19.667 --> 00:16:22.726
"By the way, he's playing a guy who's almost
always purple."

